	Posted: Sun Nov 01, 2026 11:05 pm (GMT 0)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="postbody"&gt;
	Attempting to run this build of Meka on my Mac (OS 26-ish), the app crashes upon startup. It complains that libfreetype.6.dylib is not in the expected path (&lt;i&gt;/opt/local/lib/libfreetype.6.dylib&lt;/i&gt;).
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
I'm a bit nooby when it comes to libraries on Mac OS. I do have freetype installed in &amp;quot;homebrew&amp;quot; (the package manager), is there not a way to let meka look for it there ? Otherwise I'll try copy-pasting it in the expected path but I think I may end up doing this for more libraries... :P
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
EDIT: I added a simlink for both libfreetype and libpng from their path in homebrew to the expected paths by meka. This was a bit annoying to do, but it launches now...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
